Stanford economist Nicholas Bloom's study of 16,000 Ctrip call-centre employees found remote workers were 13% more productive, took fewer sick days, and had higher job satisfaction than their in-office counterparts.
Microsoft's 2022 Work Trend Index found remote workers save an average of 72 minutes per day in commute time; 54% redirect that time to focused work.
Office workers are interrupted on average every 3.5 minutes and take 23 minutes to fully regain focus — a 2008 University of California Irvine study that has been widely replicated.
Automattic (WordPress) has been fully remote since 2005 with 2,000+ employees across 96 countries and consistently ranks among the highest-productivity software companies per employee.
